 "summary": "The crouch silhouette, the arm/leg opposition and the loop seam values are right, but the legs do not work as a walk on a floor. At each contact pose the front foot hangs 0.12 studs in the air while the rear foot is 0.18 under the floor, so no root height can ground both; the stance foot eases to a stop at every contact instead of sliding back steadily; and the planted foot swivels with the pelvis twist. The upper body is frozen apart from a 20 degree shoulder swing keyed on frame 20. Fixes: stance legs re-keyed so the sole stays flat on the floor and travels back at a constant 0.035 studs/frame for 24 frames (4 frames of double support), a heel peel and a clean swing with a soft, flat landing, hip counter-twist, a small weight shift over the stance foot, staggered arms/chest/head, then plant_feet as a safety net. Dry run of these ops on a scratch copy: 0 penetration frames, 0 slide segments, 0 seam issues, overlap 1.0.",
