   "observation": "Feet through the floor and skating for most of the cycle. Side view F000-F006 and F033-F040: the rear (blue) foot and shin are cut by the floor line; F013-F026 the same for the orange leg. Metrics: LeftFoot under the floor on 14 frames (F013-F026, down to -0.189 at F022), RightFoot on 15 frames (F000-F006, F033-F040, -0.181), shins down to -0.235. At the contact poses (F000, F020) the front foot is 0.118 ABOVE the floor while the rear foot is at -0.178, a 0.30 stud mismatch that no root offset can fix: the front leg (thigh -75, knee 85) is 0.30 shorter than the rear leg (thigh -35, knee 80), so plant_feet alone would leave the leading foot floating at contact. The planted foot also does not move back at a steady rate: every leg channel has an extreme on frames 0 and 20, so the stance foot decelerates to a stop at each contact (contact segments: mean 0.034-0.041 studs/frame with std 0.020-0.021, i.e. +-50-60%; whole-body speed falls from ~20 to 3.0 deg/frame at F019/F039). With playback scaled to ground speed that reads as the foot alternately slipping and sticking. Fix: clear the old interior leg keys and re-key the stance leg from a 2-bone IK solve so the sole is flat (Foot rx = -(thigh + knee)), on the floor, and the ankle travels back linearly at 0.035 studs/frame from 0.80 studs in front of the root; stance lasts 24 frames per foot (left 0-24, right 20-44) which gives 4 frames of double support. Root height becomes a gentle bob, lowest just after each contact (frames 2, 22) and highest at the passing pose (12, 32), with half the old range so the head stays steady. plant_feet runs last as a safety net (dry run: max correction 0.009 studs).",
