   "observation": "The step has no readable lift-off or touch-down. Lift-off: the trailing foot stays flat and slides forward under the floor (right foot F000-F006, left F020-F026, z -0.18 to -0.09) before it pops up; there is no heel peel, although the ankle is already at its -45 limit. Landing: the swing foot is still 0.12 above the floor on the frame the spec calls contact (left F000/F040, right F020) and only reaches the floor 3 frames later (left foot z 0.119, 0.099, 0.055, 0.010 on F000-F003) while it is already moving backward, so the foot lands late and drags. Fix: heel peel over the last 8 frames of stance (toe stays planted and keeps sliding, heel rises to 22 deg at lift-off on frame 24 left / 4 right), then a 16-frame swing with the knee folding to ~130 deg, 0.20-0.24 studs of toe clearance, the foot levelling out before it comes down, and the forward travel easing so the foot touches down flat with zero vertical speed and already matching ground speed (a careful, sneaking step). These keys are the swing half of the same IK solve as cwalk-1, so the seam at frame 0/40 stays closed.",
